Contract text adopted in orb-j2i.2 (VEN-C31) replaces parts of this bead's plan; where they differ, the contract governs.
- Scene entries carry Orbit's identity number and one of three states: ready, pending or unavailable. They do not carry a Kitty image id and generation pair or a separate pending marker.
- Validation before allocation:
  - an identity greater than every earlier one;
  - one incomplete resource per terminal;
  - RGB or RGBA, 1 to 4,096 pixels per side;
  - byte length = width x height x bytes per pixel, at most 10,000,000;
  - chunk count = length / 262,144 rounded up;
  - fewer than 1,024 announced and unretired, counting resources Venus freed.
- Chunks carry identity and index, are exact-size except the last, and arrive in order.
- Retirements must name a completely received, unretired resource. No resource message may precede the first frame.
- One resource per terminal is assembled and then uploaded or refused before the next announcement is accepted. "Uploaded" means the GPU has finished the copy and released its staging, so this bead and orb-j2i.11 share that rule.

